--TEST--
A shape key `Core\Db::open` requires and the settings literal omits is refused at the call, because ADR 0135 § 3 flattens a key into an argument and a missing one is a call an argument short — E0402
--FILE--
<?nvs
// `driver` is the one key both arms of `Db\Settings` require, so it is the one
// the merged list requires: the server arm and the SQLite arm disagree about
// every other field, and a key only one arm needs is not a key the call is
// short of. ADR 0135 § 2's arm selection is what will sharpen that, and until
// it lands this is the boundary.
Core\Db::open({
    host: "db.example.test",
    database: "shop",
    user: "app",
    password: "hunter2",
});
--EXPECTF-ERROR--
error[E0402]: this member requires the shape key `driver`
   --> %s:7:15
   |
 7 | Core\Db::open({
   |               ^... `driver` is not given
   | (continues to line 12)
   = help: the keys this member requires are: driver

error: aborting due to 1 error
